.SS "\fBicon_list\fP* icon_list_new (const char * name, void * theme, void * canvas, int wpad, int hpad, int flags)"
.PP
create new icon-list 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP - name for the icon-list (evidence: 'iconview' or 'shelf') 
.br
\fItheme\fP - the theme for this icon-list 
.br
\fIcanvas\fP - the canvas for this icon-list (GtkGEvas, Evas, ...) 
.br
\fIwpad\fP - horizontal padding between icons 
.br
\fIhpad\fP - vertical padding between icons 
.br
\fIflags\fP - reserved
.RE
.PP

.SS "void icon_list_resized (\fBicon_list\fP * il, long w, long h)"
.PP
adjust size of icon-list. 
.PP
the GUI-part of the icon-list will likely have a callback for when the window's size changes. that callback should in turn call icon_list_resized to let the internal representation know about the change as well. \fBicon_list_resized()\fP will also re-layout the window's contents. 
.PP
\fBParameters:\fP
.RS 4
\fIil\fP - the icon-list 
.br
\fIw\fP - the new width of the icon-list 
.br
\fIh\fP - the new height of the icon-list
.RE
.PP

.SS "int icon_list_resort (\fBicon_list\fP * il)"
.PP
